#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""haki-discord-bot: read-only slash commands about a haki server.

    /status   everything at a glance          /host     CPU, RAM, disks, temperatures
    /alerts   what's failing, last 7 days     /guests   VMs and containers
    /site     your website, live              /backup   the USB backup
    /ollama   models, GPU, live               /notes    Obsidian sync
    /help

It only reads: /run/haki-bot/snapshot.json (written by haki-snapshot as root every minute) and,
live, your site and the ollama API. Nothing it does can change the server. It connects out to
Discord's gateway, so no port is opened. Only the bot's owner (or HAKI_BOT_OWNERS) gets answers,
and every answer is visible only to the person who asked.

    haki-discord-bot                        run (systemd, as user haki-bot)
    haki-discord-bot --render <cmd> [--snapshot FILE] [--offline] [--text]
                                            print one answer without Discord (tests, terminal)

The token comes from systemd (LoadCredential=token) and is never logged.
Installed by `haki install discord-bot`; see modules/discord-bot in the haki repo.
"""
